  - line: 139
    type: narration
    text: "```"
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt gasped, back in the library, Kyh's hands on his temples."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "The sphere was still there—real, solid, warm in his palms."
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's eyes went wide."
  - line: 145
    type: narration
    text: "\"What... what is that?\""
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "The Dragon Mail hummed, Zaron's voice reverent: \"The Moon Queen's final gift."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "The seed of what must come.\""
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stared at the sphere, feeling its pulse synchronize with his heartbeat."
  - line: 152
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"She said less than three thousand years,\""
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh looked from the sphere to his face."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "\"She gave you a child?\""
  - line: 157
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"No. She gave me... a future.\""
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "He closed his hands around it. \"Something the Queen can't rewrite. A story already written, waiting to happen.\""
  - line: 160
    type: narration
    text: "The Archivist's motes swirled closer."
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "\"You hold prophecy itself, Geralt."
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "Protect it."
  - line: 163
    type: narration
    text: "When the time comes, you'll know where it must go.\""
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood, the sphere warm against his chest, the Dragon Mail settling around him with newfound purpose."
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "Less than three thousand years."
  - line: 169
    type: narration
    text: "A countdown had begun."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "end of chapter 054-tue lunar spire"

